WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.040
Good morning John; I am extremely excited
to announce that today, with the hard work

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.860
of Nerdfighteria — and, I might add, with
some amazing detective work by you — we

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:12.019
have tracked down Gussie Audrey Horsey Gowen
Manlove Brown.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:14.530
We also learned a lot of things about the
past, including the fact that there used to

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.950
be a lot of women named Gussie.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.180
[singing] Where have all the Gussies gone?

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.911
[spoken] So, starting with a marriage record
of the two people found on the tombstone,

00:00:20.911 --> 00:00:25.789
we were able to devise that Gussie used to
be Gussie Audrey Horsey; Gussie Horsey, of

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:28.740
course, being the worst possible name for
a young lady.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.800
But interestingly, in her marriage license
to Walter Manlove, she was listed as a divorcée.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.050
Well, it turns out that her family took on
boarders, and one of those boarders was a

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.039
28-year-old man named Charles Gowen. Gussie,
at that time, was 16 years old.

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:43.800
[singing] Don't stand so close to Gussie...

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.820
[spoken] Through some amazing detective work,
we have discovered that Gussie and Charles

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:52.199
R Gowen had a baby daughter named Mary. She
was born in 1901 when Gussie was 17 or 18,

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:54.289
just after they got married.

00:00:54.289 --> 00:00:58.149
They divorced soon after the birth of Mary,
and Charles kept custody of the girl.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:01.780
[singing] Little Gussie, what have you done?

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:06.090
[spoken] This marks her first two name changes:
During the marriage, to Gussie Audrey Gowen;

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.360
and then after the marriage, to Gussie Gowen
Horsey.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.790
Gussie, perhaps because of her divorce, figured
that she was never gonna get married, and

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:16.240
so she took up a trade. She became a typesetter,
something that she did for a long time in

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.240
her life.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.650
But then, in 1911, ten years later, when she
was 28 years old, she did find a man. She

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.740
found Walter Manlove. Now, Gussie is Gussie
Gowen Manlove.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.260
And then, tragedy struck. Four years after
their marriage, Walter died of tuberculosis,

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.430
resulting in the tombstone that started this
whole search.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:35.240
Gussie had, by now, changed her name again
to Gussie Audrey Manlove.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.490
Then, for ten years after the death of Walter
Manlove she lived in boarding houses with

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.680
other single women, working as a typesetter,
and at one point suing a mattress salesman.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.079
[singing] Will Gussie be... all by herself?

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:51.480
[spoken] During this period, she changed her
name again — this time, her first name — going

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.229
by Audrey G Manlove instead of Gussie A Manlove.

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:57.200
It's like she's messing with us!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.979
[singing] They call me Gussie, say I'm a Horsey,
Manlove, or Gowen; always the same. That's

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:02.920
not my name...

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.649
[spoken] But then, in 1927, Gussie married
again, to a man named James Earl Brown.

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:10.590
This marks the final name change of Gussie,
to Audrey G Brown.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:14.030
Using all of this information that we figured
out, John Green was able to find the obituary

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:17.700
and the final resting place of Audrey G Brown,
our Gussie.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.000
They bought a house together in a nice neighborhood
in Indianapolis. They lived in that house

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.070
the rest of their lives.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:27.140
Their house is now for sale... and you can
go on the Internet and look at the pictures

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.610
of the inside of that house, and it is very
strange.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.731
And if you want, you can buy that house, and
you could be a part of this very strange,

00:02:33.731 --> 00:02:36.890
long, epic story of Gussie Audrey Horsey Gowen
Manlove Brown.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.800
[singing] Gussie Audrey Horsey Gowen Manlove
Brown, we found a grave that wasn't yours

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:54.460
in Knightstown-town, so we did a lotta research,
and we tracked you down. I hope that you don't

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:55.460
mind our... pokin' around.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.700
[spoken] Thank you to John and all of the
nerdfighters in Your Pants who worked hard

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:02.110
tirelessly, hours and hours of time, to track
down all of the fascinating information about

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:04.560
this woman's life... proving, once again,
that everything is more complicated than it

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.750
at first appears.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:09.810
But if you live in Miami, Seattle, or Portland,
something isn't complicated: You should come

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:10.810
see me play a show.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.760
That is right; I have scheduled a Miami show
and it's coming up very soon, on the evening

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.200
of March 8th, Tuesday.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.900
The reason I am going to be in Miami is somewhat
complicated and I don't have time to discuss

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:21.870
it right now. Really. But basically, I am
going to be going with water.org to Haiti,

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:26.540
and I have a night — an evening — in Miami
in which I'm not doing anything, so I decided,

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:30.250
"Heck, I should rent a planetarium and play
a show!"

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:35.820
Seriously. I'm playing a show at the Miami
Science Museum, in their planetarium! I am

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:36.950
so geekin' out about this!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:42.100
But since it costs some money to rent a planetarium,
it does cost money to get into the planetarium

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.870
to see the show, and there is a link for those
of you who are in south Florida to buy tickets

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.400
to come and see me in Miami.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:52.099
Exciting stuff going on throughout Nerdfighteria.
John, I will see you on Monday.

